<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 15 September, from 994 to 1950.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">994 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,032 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Fatimids defeat the Byzantines at the Battle of the Orontes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Forces of the Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, the Turkish general Manjutakin, defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> and their Hamdanid allies under Michael Bourtzes on the Orontes.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1462">1462 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">564 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lesbos surrenders to the Ottoman sultan Mehmed II</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Niccolò <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gattilusio">Gattilusio</a>, the last Gattilusio lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesbos">Lesbos</a>, surrendered the island's capital Mytilene to the besieging Ottoman army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a>. The conquest ended the Genoese lordship of the Gattilusio family in the northeastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British troops land at Kip's Bay and take New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a heavy naval bombardment, British forces landed on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a> at Kip's Bay, sending American troops fleeing. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> stayed in British hands until 1783.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1830">1830 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">196 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Liverpool and Manchester Railway opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first inter-city railway relying wholly on steam locomotives opened with great ceremony. The day was marred when the MP William Huskisson was struck and killed by Stephenson's Rocket.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1835">1835 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">191 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">HMS Beagle reaches the Galápagos Islands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-darwin">Charles Darwin</a> spent five weeks studying the islands' finches, tortoises and mockingbirds. His observations later helped shape his theory of evolution by natural selection.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tanks go into battle for the first time on the Somme</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British Mark I tanks supported an attack at Flers-Courcelette. Many broke down, but those that advanced showed the potential of armoured warfare.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The RAF repels massed daylight raids on Battle of Britain Day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luftwaffe">Luftwaffe</a> launched two huge raids on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> and lost around 60 aircraft. Two days later Hitler postponed his planned invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> indefinitely.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1950">1950 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">76 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">UN forces land at Inchon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">US Marines led General MacArthur's amphibious landing at Inchon, far behind North Korean lines. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seoul">Seoul</a> was retaken within two weeks and the North Korean army collapsed.</p></div></li></ol>
